# ── RoofersLabs web — PRODUCTION ────────────────────────────────────────────
# You almost certainly do not want to create this file.
#
# Vite loads `.env.production` for ANY `vite build`, so a copy of it on a laptop
# silently changes what every local build produces. The deployed builds do not
# use it: infra/scripts/deploy-web.sh exports VITE_API_BASE_URL and
# VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY from the target environment's Terraform outputs,
# and process environment wins over env files in Vite. That is what guarantees
# the production bundle points at the production API and the development bundle
# at the development one — a property of the build, not a habit.
#
# The values production is built with:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL           https://api.rooferslabs.com
#                               (envs/production → `terraform output api_url`)
#   VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY  the production Clerk instance's pk_…
#                               (envs/production → `terraform output clerk_publishable_key`)
#
# To ship the frontend, run the script — never `npm run build` on its own:
#
#   infra/scripts/deploy-web.sh production
#
# For local work, use .env.development.example.
